ayload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8d0175ab0a93bea509094b26f24128e3370a40e72eba269502d961f28bbc1a4a","event_uuid":"cc1e289d-d1f1-4df5-8323-46ea2afd8bdd","position":{"commit_sha":"5a57f0e212373c0cd379270b07b2e20f9adf8bfd","position":"1788130078341803987-cc1e289d-d1f1-4df5-8323-46ea2afd8bdd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e2beb58314b1c25bfed740fe587506cd2e098a6b75b1fc0d3a54a6e8299e0877","event_uuid":"c2c25591-e0d1-4d5e-a183-ba0c06cf648e","position":{"commit_sha":"8ca6f6fd2e29eb608cd73b48be4333de339bc949","position":"1788131470651649715-c2c25591-e0d1-4d5e-a183-ba0c06cf648e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Dependency notice: typed-payload implementation now waits for both headroom prerequisites: existing `wormlike-buried-grunion` and new `piscine-bullish-cowbird`. Its typed outputs and portable parity oracle then become prerequisites for `gnarled-wraithlike-flatfish`, which owns producer-input convergence before final cutover.","timestamp":1788055577525868243},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Approved intentional deltas (typed vs. legacy payload shadow comparison)\n\nPer AC5 (\"Each intentional delta has a named test, rationale, and approval\nrecorded on the ticket\"), the shadow corpus (`tests/fixtures/reconciler/\npayload_corpus/v1/`) documents 4 approved intentional deltas between the\nlegacy dict payload shape and the ADR 0107 typed contract — each backed by\na named `expect: \"reject\"` scenario and asserted in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_payload_shadow_corpus.py`:\n\n1. **`inbound_conflict_legacy_shape_has_no_payload_reason`** — today's live\n   `differ.py` inbound-conflict producers put `reason` in\n   `Mutation.provenance` and ship payload={} or {\"jira_field_snapshot\":...},\n   never `reason`/`jira_key` IN the payload. ADR 0107's decision table\n   requires `InboundConflictPayload(reason, jira_key)` in the payload. The\n   typed contract intentionally rejects today's legacy shape — reconciling\n   `differ.py`'s producers is the ADR's deferred \"Cut\" step (AC7).\n2. **`outbound_delete_rejects_stray_field`** / **`outbound_probe_rejects_stray_field`**\n   — ADR 0107 defect #2: today nothing stops an `(outbound, delete)`/\n   `(outbound, probe)` Mutation from carrying a stray extra payload key. The\n   typed contract now rejects any nonempty payload for these two actions at\n   construction time — this is the mechanism behind AC1's \"construction\n   rejects ... extra critical ... fields before effects\".\n3. **`outbound_update_rejects_empty_payload`** — an `(outbound, update)`\n   Mutation with an all-excluded, empty `{}` payload is constructible today;\n   the typed contract requires at least one of\n   `changed_fields`/`comments`/`labels`/`links` nonempty — a no-op update is\n   not a meaningful Mutation under the typed contract.\n4. **`inbound_delete_and_probe_are_dead_by_design`** — `(inbound, delete)`/\n   `(inbound, probe)` are allowed by `_VALID_COMBINATIONS` but never\n   registered by `typed_dispatch._LEAVES` and never constructed in\n   production (ADR 0028 / bug 3b5f). Per this ticket's own task boundary,\n   this story deliberately does NOT model a payload type for either pair —\n   narrowing `_VALID_COMBINATIONS` is bug 3b5f's job, out of scope here.\n\nAlso noted (pre-existing, NOT new defects, left as-is per AC7's\nno-producer-rewiring scope):\n- `differ.py`'s older `_compute_mutations_emit_both` outbound-update path\n  emits a flat unwrapped `changed` dict as payload, while\n  `outbound_pass.py`/`binding_walk.py` wrap it as\n  `{\"changed_fields\": {...}, ...}` — two different legacy shapes for the\n  same `(outbound, update)` pair already coexist in production.\n- `binding_walk.py`'s inbound-create ADOPT path emits\n  `{\"fields\":..., \"jira_fields\":...}` while `differ.py`'s inbound-create\n  path emits a flat dict with no wrapper key; `apply_inbound.py`'s\n  `_apply_inbound_create` leaf already explicitly tolerates both shapes.\n\nFull provenance/versioning/normalization-rule documentation lives in\n`tests/fixtures/reconciler/payload_corpus/README.md`.","timestamp":1788109187216395001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"BLOCKED on landing (not on implementation): Gerrit change #2436 (typed mutation payload union + comparator) has LLM-Review +1 (PASS) but Verified has failed 5 consecutive CI runs, all on the identical single test tests/unit/test_audit_serve_heldout.py::test_serve_binds_loopback_ephemeral_and_lists_ticket (\"Network access is forbidden...\"), across all 3 Python versions each time.\n\nThis is a pre-existing flake unrelated to this change's files (mutation_payloads.py, payload_shadow.py, mutation.py share no code/imports/fixtures with the audit-serve test). Root-caused and tracked separately as ignitable-noteworthy-osprey (edeb-c3ad-c051-4e6a, discovered_from this ticket). Evidence: passes 100% in isolation locally; reproduces identically under CI's exact full-suite -n4 --dist worksteal invocation locally; an unrelated dependency-sweep CI job also failed in the same time window with a completely different signature, consistent with shared-runner contention.\n\nPer AGENTS.md's flaky-test policy (root-cause, don't blindly retry), I stopped after 5 identical failures rather than continue rechecking. This ticket's own dependency change (#2435, the corpus) is already MERGED. Change #2436 needs a human operator to either fix/quarantine the flaky audit-serve test or make the call on landing #2436 despite it (a repo-admin decision I cannot make). All implementation, tests, corpus, and gates for e9d5 itself are complete and green locally (lint, typecheck, complexity ratchet, module-size, full regression suite). The ticket cannot be transitioned to closed until #2436 is Verified +1 and merged (the completion-verifier's file-impact check requires a commit for this ticket reachable from origin/main).","timestamp":1788120007469010001}],"created_at":1788026443688325591,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7a110fb0-0528-4bef-a7bb-93bb84e3e7be","relation":"blocks","target_id":"3f27-cb3c-8023-4f57"},{"link_uuid":"dec01173-a7d6-4fb2-b080-0be775d5a0c4","relation":"blocks","target_id":"6452-715f-21c9-4285"},{"link_uuid":"bc3cef11-8bb0-423e-ac67-0f4a5a2fdd6e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"23b7-cb37-14d1-454e"},{"link_uuid":"2409e581-2504-401e-a4d9-0d8dadc7b2ac","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"89c9-3056-8b4c-4696"},{"link_uuid":"cc1e289d-d1f1-4df5-8323-46ea2afd8bdd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fec7-5188-2c84-4fdf"},{"link_uuid":"c2c25591-e0d1-4d5e-a183-ba0c06cf648e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"00c5-a490-eaf9-4d60"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nImplement the contract decided by the preceding architecture story without changing the production write route yet. The key deliverable is sufficient deterministic parity evidence to make the later cutover/deletion safe within this epic.\n\nExisting useful assets include the real store-copy scrub/isolation fixtures, canonical serialization, route census, verified Cloud/DC fakes, and comprehensive mutation tests. Reuse them rather than creating a parallel reconciler harness.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Introduce the approved direction/action payload union and thread it through planner and coordinator boundaries up to a side-effect-free adapter projection seam.\n- Build a versioned corpus from deterministic synthetic tickets plus a scrubbed representative store snapshot. Include edge and failure shapes, not credentials or live bindings.\n- Drive legacy and typed planning/serialization over identical observations. Capture canonical normalized intent/outcome traces without invoking either writer.\n- Compare ordering, fields, identity scopes, diagnostics, follow-ons, suppression, retry dispositions, and modeled final state.\n- Run this oracle in default portable CI with no Jira, Docker, external service, or CI-provider dependency.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — typed payloads and the effect-free trace projection.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — portable replay and verified adapter contracts.\n- `tests/fixtures/` — versioned synthetic/scrubbed corpus with no credentials or live bindings.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: representative inbound and outbound mutations produce matching normalized legacy/typed traces and modeled state. Edge/failure paths: malformed payloads, ambiguous commits, exhaustion, suppression, follow-ons, and cross-project routes either match or produce an approved named delta. Effect spies fail if the shadow path reaches Jira, the ticket store, a subprocess, clock sleep, or network.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Planners and coordinator use named payload types for every supported direction/action pair; construction rejects missing, extra critical, or wrong-action fields before effects.\n- [ ] The shadow comparator executes no Jira transport or ticket-store write, proven with failing spies on every effect seam.\n- [ ] The corpus covers create/update/delete/probe/conflict, inbound-only actions, links/comments/labels/status/parent/assignee/binding fields, duplicate and malformed inputs, suppression/follow-ons, ambiguous outcomes, retry exhaustion, and multi-project routing.\n- [ ] Replaying the same corpus is deterministic and idempotent; corpus version/provenance and normalization rules are explicit.\n- [ ] Legacy and typed traces have zero unexplained differences. Each intentional delta has a named test, rationale, and approval recorded on the ticket.\n- [ ] Verified-fake Jira Cloud and Data Center adapter contract tests pass without selecting a live backend.\n- [ ] Production continues to use the pre-cutover route in this story: the story's diff touches no production dispatch entry point (`typed_dispatch._LEAVES`, `batch_dispatch._mutation_to_batch_dict`, `applier.apply()`, or any producer in `differ.py` / `outbound_mutation_builders.py` / `run_differs.py` / `outbound_pass.py` / `binding_walk.py` / `invariants.py`) — verified by an explicit route-census check (a test asserting each of those callables is byte-identical / import-reachable and unmodified in this change) — and no module introduced by this story is later relied upon as a permanent production write path (verified by: every new module lives under the shadow-only seam named in Scope, is exercised only by tests, and is not imported by any of the production entry points just named).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/","reason":"Typed payload union and side-effect-free trace projection."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/","reason":"Portable legacy-versus-typed shadow replay."},{"path":"tests/fixtures/","reason":"Versioned synthetic/scrubbed replay corpus."}],"file_impact_scope"